# Line endings.
#
# Several gates assert that a committed file is byte-identical to what its generator produces —
# the GAIA panel and profile, the three QA sheets, the visual goldens. Generators write LF. Git on
# Windows checks a text file out as CRLF by default, so on a Windows clone every one of those gates
# failed with a diff in which actual and expected were otherwise identical.
#
# The tests fold CRLF themselves (CE/web/test/support/readText.mjs) so a clone made before this
# file existed still passes. This keeps the working tree LF so the two never drift apart again, and
# so regenerating on Windows produces no phantom whole-file diff.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated artefacts and goldens: never touched by hand, compared byte for byte.
*.cepanel                     text eol=lf
*.ceditor-device.json         text eol=lf
CE/web/test/golden/*.txt      text eol=lf

# Binaries, so nothing tries to normalize them.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ico    binary
*.wasm   binary
*.exe    binary
